WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.005
You do not need a phone, or Android Studio, or Xcode.

2
00:00:04.005 --> 00:00:09.825
In a few minutes, you can have a real app running on a simulated phone, in your browser.

3
00:00:11.425 --> 00:00:12.056
Step one.

4
00:00:12.056 --> 00:00:14.438
Open a terminal and make your app.

5
00:00:14.438 --> 00:00:16.820
Type npx shipvo init, then a name.

6
00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:19.063
Shipvo also makes a signing key.

7
00:00:19.063 --> 00:00:21.375
Keep it safe, and never share it.

8
00:00:22.975 --> 00:00:23.645
Step two.

9
00:00:23.645 --> 00:00:25.357
Go into the new folder.

10
00:00:25.357 --> 00:00:30.643
Run npm install, and then install the small browser the simulator uses.

11
00:00:30.643 --> 00:00:33.100
The second one takes the longest.

12
00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:35.697
Step three.

13
00:00:35.697 --> 00:00:37.147
Run npm run sim.

14
00:00:37.147 --> 00:00:42.222
Wait for the line that says Simulator on localhost:4545.

15
00:00:42.222 --> 00:00:46.844
Then open your browser at localhost:4545/app/.

16
00:00:46.844 --> 00:00:49.200
Your app is on the screen.

17
00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:52.584
Click Send a notification.

18
00:00:52.584 --> 00:00:54.299
The log says it was sent.

19
00:00:54.299 --> 00:00:55.945
Nothing really went out.

20
00:00:55.945 --> 00:00:59.375
The simulator labels everything it pretends to do.

21
00:01:00.975 --> 00:01:01.656
Step four.

22
00:01:01.656 --> 00:01:02.813
Change the words.

23
00:01:02.813 --> 00:01:06.421
Open src/release.ts, and edit the headline.

24
00:01:06.421 --> 00:01:10.029
Save the file, wait for "rebuilt", and reload the page.

25
00:01:10.029 --> 00:01:12.275
Your new words are on the screen.

26
00:01:13.875 --> 00:01:14.584
Step five.

27
00:01:14.584 --> 00:01:15.719
Check a release.

28
00:01:15.719 --> 00:01:18.698
Run shipvo publish --dry-run.

29
00:01:18.698 --> 00:01:22.386
Shipvo builds and signs your app, but sends nothing.

30
00:01:22.386 --> 00:01:23.875
So it is safe to try.

31
00:01:25.475 --> 00:01:26.973
That is your first app.

32
00:01:26.973 --> 00:01:32.575
The full guide, with every command, is at shipvo.dev/docs/first-app.
